WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.070
In Yosemite stands Lembert
Dome, a dome of bare bedrock.

2
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.030
Walk up one side, and the slope is gentle.

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.530
Reach the top, and the other
side drops away as a steep face.

4
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.690
One rock, two very different sides.

5
00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.450
Did a river cut one side?

6
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.150
Did wind wear it down?

7
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.950
Did an earthquake split it?

8
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.170
So why is Lembert Dome so lopsided?

9
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.190
In this mission, you'll find
out how solid rock is worn away,

10
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.790
picked up, carried and dropped.

11
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.490
Then you'll learn to read a landform's
shape for clues to how it formed.

12
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:40.770
Your mission: explain why Lembert Dome
has a gentle slope on one side and a steep

13
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.030
face on the other.
